From 35935bde089bbd4d1be97163d1e5ba87d5d4f145 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: spotUP <retroranksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:42:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] upkg: the xsystem comment says how a forwarded SIGINT reaches
 curl

The comment called curl a native clib2 program and said ixemul kill() sends
SIGBREAKF_CTRL_C to a non-ixemul task. curl is an ixemul program that waits
in a native bsdsocket WaitSelect; kill() left its SIGINT pending until
ixemul-vtcon 627d6ce, which sends the Ctrl-C break to such a wait. Comment
only.
---
 libopkg/xsystem.c | 16 +++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libopkg/xsystem.c b/libopkg/xsystem.c
index 7949e89..eff2bba 100644
--- a/libopkg/xsystem.c
+++ b/libopkg/xsystem.c
@@ -63,13 +63,15 @@ int upkg_xsystem_is_unattended(void)
 
 /* Waiting for the child. ixemul's wait4 sleeps in a loop that never returns EINTR, and its sleep eats
    the Ctrl-C break (clears SIGBREAKF_CTRL_C) whether or not a SIGINT reaches this task, so a Ctrl-C
-   sent to upkg was lost and upkg sat in waitpid until the child (curl, a native clib2 program that
-   may ignore the break itself) finished: 23 to 25 s against a stalled server. So never block in wait4:
-   poll with WNOHANG and nap with the dos.library Delay (which leaves the break set), and look for a
-   break or a SIGINT between polls. On a break: forward it to the child (ixemul kill() sends
-   SIGBREAKF_CTRL_C to a non-ixemul task), give the child UPKG_BREAK_GRACE seconds to leave, then
-   stop waiting. A child that ignores the break is left running (it exits when its transfer ends or
-   when curl honours Ctrl-C); upkg itself ends at once with the exit code of an interrupted program. */
+   sent to upkg was lost and upkg sat in waitpid until the child (curl, an ixemul program that waits
+   for the network in a native bsdsocket WaitSelect) finished: 23 to 25 s against a stalled server.
+   So never block in wait4: poll with WNOHANG and nap with the dos.library Delay (which leaves the
+   break set), and look for a break or a SIGINT between polls. On a break: forward SIGINT to the child
+   with kill() (ixemul-vtcon 627d6ce and later turn a pending SIGINT into SIGBREAKF_CTRL_C for a task
+   waiting natively on that break; curl ends its transfer on it since pkgs/curl patch 0003), give the
+   child UPKG_BREAK_GRACE seconds to leave, then stop waiting. A child that ignores the break is left
+   running (it exits when its transfer ends); upkg itself ends at once with the exit code of an
+   interrupted program. */
 #define UPKG_BREAK_GRACE 3
 #define UPKG_NAP_MS 50
 
